  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Macroeconomic Resilience Program, Subprogram 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program, consisting of three subprograms, aims to strengthen Tonga&apos;s long-term
growth prospects and capacity to respond to external shocks. It supports government efforts to
improve (i) its fiscal position by adopting prudent policies and better public financial management
(PFM); and (ii) the business climate by continuing policy, regulatory, and public enterprise reforms.
Subprogram 3 is the final subprogram, and builds on progress under two earlier subprograms of
the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and other development partners approved in fiscal year (FY)
2016 and FY2017. 1 The program is consistent with ADB&apos;s Strategy 2030 priority of strengthening
governance and institutional capacity, particularly in small island developing states.</narrative>
  </description>
